# SOC 2 Type II evidence: ten controls tested over six months of exports,
# for Brindlewood, a payroll company a month from fieldwork. The period is
# 2026-01-01 to 2026-06-30.
#
# B, D-F and I are commands (checks/controls.py) that re-perform each
# control's test over the files in evidence/, applying the policies' own
# allowances (a Standard change, a cancelled ticket, a retest within 7 days,
# a risk acceptance approved before the due date), so every count can be
# run again for the auditor. C, G and H are agent cells: which files test
# the control, whether a deviation is one our policy allows, and whether the
# evidence covers the whole period (a single snapshot of a continuous
# control may not, which is worth the auditor's attention). J is the result,
# computed from the counts: Evidence missing only when nothing tests it. K is a second
# agent re-performing the test from the files without seeing the counts,
# and L says whether it agrees. evidence_untouched checks that nothing
# under evidence/ changed.
#
# Select C2:K11 and Run Selection to fill the agent cells. The company,
# people and exports are synthetic.
instructions = You are on Brindlewood's security team preparing for SOC 2 Type II fieldwork; the audit period is 2026-01-01 to 2026-06-30, by the UTC date of each record. documents/controls.csv lists the controls, evidence/ holds the exports, and policies/ our policies; apply the policies' own definitions and allowances. Never change anything in evidence/ or policies/. Answer in exactly the form the question asks for, with no preamble; cite the passage your answer rests on with cite_cell. If nothing in evidence/ shows the control operated, say so: Not found, or No for a yes/no question.
A1 = Control
B1 = Owner
C1 = Evidence files used: the files under evidence/ that test this control, comma-separated, or Not found
D1 = Population (check)
E1 = Exceptions (check)
F1 = Exception details (check)
G1 = Is a deviation from this control one our policy allows, and did one occur in the period (a risk acceptance, a retest, a Standard change)? Yes or No
H1 = Does the evidence cover the whole period? Yes or No
I1 = Latest evidence date (check)
J1 = Result
K1 = Re-perform this control's test yourself from the files in evidence/ and the policy, without reading any other cell on the board: answer as population/exceptions, for example 120/2, or Not found
L1 = Re-performance
A2 = CC8.1-PR: Code change review
B2 = $ python3 checks/controls.py owner CC8.1-PR
D2 = $ python3 checks/controls.py population CC8.1-PR # watch: evidence/**
E2 = $ python3 checks/controls.py exceptions CC8.1-PR # watch: evidence/**
F2 = $ python3 checks/controls.py details CC8.1-PR # watch: evidence/**
I2 = $ python3 checks/controls.py latest CC8.1-PR # watch: evidence/**
C2 = @claude('{instructions} Control: {$A2}. {C$1}')
G2 = @claude('{instructions} Control: {$A2}. {G$1}')
H2 = @claude('{instructions} Control: {$A2}. {H$1}')
K2 = @claude('{instructions} Control: {$A2}. {K$1}')
J2 = = if({D2} == 'Not found', 'Evidence missing', if({E2} > 0, 'Exception noted', 'Effective'))
L2 = = if({K2} == '', '', if(or({K2} == concat({D2}, '/', {E2}), and({D2} == 'Not found', {K2} == 'Not found')), 'agree', 'disagree'))
